                <h1 class="content-title">SAM Pro <span class="gradient-text">Data Model & Architecture</span></h1>
                <p class="content-subtitle">
                    The foundation of SAM Pro is an intricate relational model connecting hardware topology and raw discovery strings to commercial software models, financial entitlement contracts, and compliance calculation results.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- 1. ERD -->
            <section class="content-section" id="erd">
                <h2>Master Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD)</h2>
                <p>
                    The data model solves a critical challenge: IT discovery tools inspect running hardware and file systems, while procurement systems process vendor SKUs and purchase contracts. The <strong>Software Model</strong> serves as the central bridge joining physical technical reality with legal contractual rights.
                </p>

                <div class="diagram-block">
                    <div class="diagram-title">SAM Pro Comprehensive Data Architecture ERD</div>
                    <div class="mermaid">
                    erDiagram
                        cmdb_ci_computer ||--o{ cmdb_sam_sw_install : "hosts"
                        cmdb_ci_esx_server ||--o{ cmdb_ci_computer : "virtualizes"
                        cmdb_ci_cluster ||--o{ cmdb_ci_esx_server : "groups"

                        cmdb_sam_sw_discovery_model ||--|{ cmdb_sam_sw_install : "normalizes"
                        cmdb_software_product_model ||--|{ cmdb_sam_sw_discovery_model : "maps via DMAP"
                        core_company ||--o{ cmdb_software_product_model : "manufactures"
                        core_company ||--o{ alm_license : "contracts with"

                        cmdb_software_product_model ||--|{ alm_license : "licensed by"
                        alm_license ||--o{ alm_entitlement_user : "allocated to"
                        sys_user ||--o{ alm_entitlement_user : "assigned"
                        alm_license ||--o{ alm_entitlement_asset : "allocated to"
                        cmdb_ci_computer ||--o{ alm_entitlement_asset : "assigned"

                        cmdb_software_product_model ||--o{ samp_reconciliation_result : "evaluates"
                        samp_reconciliation_result ||--|{ samp_license_metric_result : "breaks down"

                        cmdb_software_product_model ||--o{ samp_sw_reclamation_rule : "governs"
                        samp_sw_reclamation_rule ||--o{ samp_sw_reclamation_candidate : "triggers"
                        sys_user ||--o{ samp_sw_reclamation_candidate : "targeted"
                        
                        sys_user ||--o{ samp_sw_subscription : "consumes cloud seat"
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="info-card info-card--important">
                    <div class="info-card-title">Inheritance & Core Scoping</div>
                    <p>
                        Understanding table inheritance is vital for developers:
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><code>alm_license</code> extends <strong><code>alm_asset</code></strong>, inheriting financial accounting, purchase orders, depreciation schedules, and asset lifecycle tracking.</li>
                        <li><code>cmdb_software_product_model</code> extends <strong><code>cmdb_model</code></strong>, allowing seamless integration with Product Catalogs and Service Catalog request items.</li>
                        <li><code>cmdb_sam_sw_install</code> extends <strong><code>cmdb_ci</code></strong>, enabling full tracking through CI relationships, CMDB health metrics, and audit history.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 2. Discovery & Install Layer -->
            <section class="content-section" id="discovery-layer">
                <h2>1. Discovery & Installation Layer</h2>
                <p>
                    This layer captures raw, unprocessed inventory from endpoints and servers, subsequently grouping them into canonical technical signatures.
                </p>

                <div class="accordion">
                    <div class="accordion-item open">
                        <button class="accordion-trigger">
                            <span class="accordion-trigger-text">Software Installations (cmdb_sam_sw_install)</span>
                            <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                        </button>
                        <div class="accordion-body">
                            <div class="accordion-content">
                                <p>Stores individual software installations detected on physical or virtual endpoints.</p>
                                <div class="data-table-wrapper">
                                    <table class="data-table">
                                        <thead>
                                            <tr>
                                                <th>Label</th>
                                                <th>Column Name</th>
                                                <th>Type</th>
                                                <th>Reference Target</th>
                                                <th>Description</th>
                                            </tr>
                                        </thead>
                                        <tbody>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Installed On</td>
                                                <td><code>installed_on</code></td>
                                                <td>Reference</td>
                                                <td><code>cmdb_ci_computer</code></td>
                                                <td>The hardware CI (laptop, server, VM) hosting the software.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Display Name</td>
                                                <td><code>display_name</code></td>
                                                <td>String</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>Raw application string extracted from registry or package manager.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Publisher</td>
                                                <td><code>publisher</code></td>
                                                <td>String</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>Raw vendor string reported by discovery before normalization.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Version</td>
                                                <td><code>version</code></td>
                                                <td>String</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>Raw version string (e.g. 15.0.2000.5).</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Discovery Model</td>
                                                <td><code>discovery_model</code></td>
                                                <td>Reference</td>
                                                <td><code>cmdb_sam_sw_discovery_model</code></td>
                                                <td>Foreign key linking this raw install to its normalized cluster.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Last Used Date</td>
                                                <td><code>last_used</code></td>
                                                <td>DateTime</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>Last launch timestamp reported by SCCM, Jamf, or ACC metering.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Usage Status</td>
                                                <td><code>usage_status</code></td>
                                                <td>Choice</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>Active (< 30 days), Low (30-60 days), Inactive (> 90 days).</td>
                                            </tr>
                                        </tbody>
                                    </table>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <button class="accordion-trigger">
                            <span class="accordion-trigger-text">Software Discovery Models (cmdb_sam_sw_discovery_model)</span>
                            <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                        </button>
                        <div class="accordion-body">
                            <div class="accordion-content">
                                <p>Groups thousands of identical raw installations into standardized canonical signatures.</p>
                                <div class="data-table-wrapper">
                                    <table class="data-table">
                                        <thead>
                                            <tr>
                                                <th>Label</th>
                                                <th>Column Name</th>
                                                <th>Type</th>
                                                <th>Reference Target</th>
                                                <th>Description</th>
                                            </tr>
                                        </thead>
                                        <tbody>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Normalized Publisher</td>
                                                <td><code>norm_publisher</code></td>
                                                <td>String</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>Clean publisher name standardized by Content Library (e.g. "Microsoft").</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Normalized Product</td>
                                                <td><code>norm_product</code></td>
                                                <td>String</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>Canonical product family name (e.g. "SQL Server").</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Normalized Version</td>
                                                <td><code>norm_version</code></td>
                                                <td>String</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>Major release version (e.g. "2019").</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Normalized Edition</td>
                                                <td><code>norm_edition</code></td>
                                                <td>String</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>Tier or edition (e.g. "Standard", "Enterprise").</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Software Model</td>
                                                <td><code>software_model</code></td>
                                                <td>Reference</td>
                                                <td><code>cmdb_software_product_model</code></td>
                                                <td>The business software model this discovery model maps to.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Normalization Status</td>
                                                <td><code>norm_status</code></td>
                                                <td>Choice</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>Normalized, Partially Normalized, Publisher Normalized, Match Not Found.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                        </tbody>
                                    </table>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 3. Catalog & Entitlements -->
            <section class="content-section" id="catalog-layer">
                <h2>2. Catalog, Modeling & Entitlement Layer</h2>
                <p>
                    This commercial layer defines what the organization owns, how software is sold, and how rights are partitioned among business units.
                </p>

                <div class="accordion">
                    <div class="accordion-item open">
                        <button class="accordion-trigger">
                            <span class="accordion-trigger-text">Software Models (cmdb_software_product_model)</span>
                            <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                        </button>
                        <div class="accordion-body">
                            <div class="accordion-content">
                                <p>The definitive commercial catalog item representing the software asset from a procurement and lifecycle perspective.</p>
                                <div class="data-table-wrapper">
                                    <table class="data-table">
                                        <thead>
                                            <tr>
                                                <th>Label</th>
                                                <th>Column Name</th>
                                                <th>Type</th>
                                                <th>Reference Target</th>
                                                <th>Description</th>
                                            </tr>
                                        </thead>
                                        <tbody>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Display Name</td>
                                                <td><code>display_name</code></td>
                                                <td>String</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>Product name (e.g. Microsoft SQL Server 2019 Standard).</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Publisher</td>
                                                <td><code>manufacturer</code></td>
                                                <td>Reference</td>
                                                <td><code>core_company</code></td>
                                                <td>The software vendor / manufacturer.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Lifecycle Phase</td>
                                                <td><code>lifecycle_phase</code></td>
                                                <td>Choice</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>General Availability, End of Support, End of Life.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>End of Life Date</td>
                                                <td><code>end_of_life</code></td>
                                                <td>Date</td>
                                                <td>—</td>
                                                <td>Publisher date where security patches permanently cease.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>Is Suite Parent</td>
